# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is ALLOWED in this repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository IS the published surface. Cloudflare Pages serves it, so a
# file being here is the same as a file being on the internet. The list below
# exists because we have already shipped twice by accident:
#
#   * README.md / .gitignore were publicly readable at the apex for days — the
#     publish root is deploy/, so the repo root was never meant to be served.
#   * A rendered explainer video with a retracted privacy caption sat at
#     /deploy/assets/social/shorts/familyos-explainer.mp4 and kept being served
#     after the copy that generated it had been fixed (#195, 2026-10-02).
#
# Nothing under .wrangler/ is ever a source asset; it is local deploy state.

.wrangler/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered social media — NOT source, NOT published
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The .mp4/.png in assets/social/ were exported by hand and committed by hand.
# They are binary, unreviewable in a diff, and they silently contradict the
# copy in deploy/index.html when the copy changes — which is exactly the 2026-10-02
# defect. The scripts that generate them are source and stay in git; the renders
# live outside the publish root (see deploy/assets/social/README.md).
#
# If you are re-adding these, stop and read deploy/assets/social/README.md first.
deploy/assets/social/**/*.mp4
deploy/assets/social/**/*.gif
deploy/assets/social/shorts/media/
